- **Production incident diagnosis** - ✅ Complete
- **Regression tests and canonical-origin contract** - ✅ Complete
- **Cache and metadata remediation** - ✅ Complete
- **Nginx, proxy, and image-probe hardening** - ✅ Complete
- **Transient-failure and template lifecycle remediation** - ✅ Complete
- **Multi-tenant rollout and recrawl verification** - 🟡 In progress

### Next Steps
- [x] Add the apex/`www`/subdomain/localhost/hostile-host/protocol/auth request-order matrix.
- [x] Implement validated canonical origins, semantic versioned metadata caching,
  complete config/content invalidation, single escaping, configured title/favicon,
  real 404/noindex handling, and side-effect-free image metadata.
- [x] Add a dedicated nginx health/default server, fail-closed host map, restricted
  provisioned-site regex, and a generated two-tenant config regression.
- [x] Update backend, caching/CDN, infrastructure, and security specifications.
- [x] 2026-07-30 verification passed: full backend and root module tests; backend
  and root `go vet`; focused affected-package race detector; affected-package and
  root staticcheck excluding the repository's pre-existing `U1000` baseline;
  backend/root builds; generated-nginx fixture; and `git diff --check`.
- [x] 2026-08-02 auditor/correctness review traced the permanent startup 404 to
  singleton handler construction plus a pre-shipped frontend, and reviewed
  commits `57f3dcb3` and `c4381994`. The manual retry is race-safe and repairs
  cached read failure, but is not final because it caches successful template
  bytes forever, bypasses `INDEX_FILE_PATH`, returns infrastructure failures as
  `404`, leaves database/config error cache poisoning possible, and removed the
  secret-bearing `backends/` Docker exclusion.
- [x] Restore the root `backends/` Docker exclusion before any build or rollout.
- [x] Implement the typed success/absence/degraded/error SEO resolution contract;
  cache only authoritative metadata or genuine absence and return uncached
  `503` for core dependency failures.
- [x] Make template loading honor `INDEX_FILE_PATH`, retry failures, return
  uncached `503`/noindex while unavailable, and observe hot-shipped replacements
  without reconstructing or restarting the handler.
- [x] Add handler-level, deterministic dependency-failure, cache-write, hot-ship,
  Docker-context, and race regressions described in Step 9 of the plan.
- [x] Update the affected specs and backend frontend-path documentation after the
  implemented behavior is verified.
- [x] 2026-08-02 regression-remediation verification passed: focused SEO/config/
  forum/store and root app tests; complete backend suite; explicit complete root
  package suite (the `./...` glob alone cannot traverse the root-owned runtime
  `postgres_data/` volume); SEO race detector and staticcheck; backend/root vet
  and builds; frontend production build; and `git diff --check`. The semantic
  cache moved to `seo:meta:v3:` so previously poisoned v2 values are never read.
- [x] 2026-08-02 local rollout follow-up reproduced the startup fallback through
  the actual `home` tenant. Its legacy `INDEX_FILE_PATH=/frontend/dist/index.html`
  survived default synchronization, and nginx's server-level `return 444`
  preempted default-server health routing. Added an exact legacy-path migration,
  corrected the nginx fallback template source, scoped unknown-host rejection to
  `location /`, and made the shared probe explicitly IPv4. Recreated `home` with
  its frontend, regenerated nginx, and verified both containers healthy plus a
  raw nginx `200` application shell without the startup fallback.
- [ ] On the production deployment host, inventory each tenant's primary domain,
  explicit aliases, `PUBLIC_BASE_URL`, `SITEMAP_BASE_URL`, and Cloudflare SSL mode.
  This checkout contains only the local `home` tenant, so that inventory cannot
  be completed here.
- [ ] Deploy the backend and control-plane changes together, run `grengo migrate
  all` to persist canonical defaults, run `grengo nginx reload`, and recreate or
